### What Sun shows without words, in pa3ds's own words, a beat at a time, said under [pa3ds.ui]
### descriptions. When each is said is `../scenes.toml`'s, every language's; a beat is found here
### by its id there (ADR-0040). A name the game shows is never written here.

# The chase after Kukui's call, demo 6, unskippable. Before it the camera leaves the monitor for
# the desk; the game says "Three months later..." itself at 71 s, and the field takes over at about
# 89 s with the arrival, which plays without the player until Mom speaks at about 114 s. The
# arrival's beats wait for the field, Route 1's zone 0x0, which came 91 s after the demo started in
# movie1_opening.ctm (2026-10-13).
chase-1 = After the call, the camera turned to your desk: a travel magazine open on pictures of tropical islands, and a plane ticket.
chase-2 = Somewhere else, a girl in a white sun hat and white dress runs through a gleaming white building, a big bag over her shoulder.
chase-3 = She stops at a railing and looks back, holding the bag close.
chase-4 = She runs on into a glass-roofed garden, along a white bridge through the trees.
chase-5 = Men in white uniforms and caps are after her. One blocks the bridge ahead.
chase-6 = They close in, one of them grinning. She stops, clutching the bag.
chase-7 = A burst of blue light flares around her.
chase-8 = A glowing ball of light rises through the glass roof into the sky.
chase-9 = The game's title logo appears.
chase-10 = From high above: a green island ringed by reefs, with a town by the harbour and an old volcano crater.
chase-11 = On the ground: a seaside lawn with palm trees and a low fence. A boy in a white shirt walks across the grass.
chase-12 = A grey wooden house on stilts, with a porch, steps and a mailbox. A small Pokémon trots by.

# Ultra Sun's chase, demo 2.
us-chase-1 = After the call, the camera turned to your desk: a travel magazine open on a picture of a gleaming white building by the sea.
us-chase-2 = Somewhere else, a girl in a white sun hat and white dress runs along a white gallery, a big bag over her shoulder.
us-chase-3 = She runs out along a walkway under a glass roof, past palm trees.
us-chase-4 = She stops and looks back, holding the bag close.
us-chase-5 = Two figures in grey and white armour, their faces behind visors, stand in her way.
us-chase-6 = They close in on her, and she backs away, clutching the bag.
us-chase-7 = A burst of blue light flares around her, and the two shield their eyes.
us-chase-8 = A glowing ball of light rises through the glass roof into the sky.
us-chase-9 = The game's title logo appears: Pokémon Ultra Sun.
us-chase-10 = From high above: a green island ringed by reefs, with a town by the harbour and an old volcano crater.
us-chase-11 = On the ground: a seaside lawn with palm trees and a low white fence, the sea beyond.
us-chase-12 = A blue wooden house with a porch, steps and flowers by the door. A small Pokémon trots by.

# Mahalo Trail's bridge: the field's demo 7, the line after "Save Nebby!", the field's demo 8, and
# the lines after it.
bridge-1 = The girl in the white sun hat runs along a dirt path towards an old wooden bridge over a gorge, a waterfall behind it.
bridge-2 = Her bag jolts in her arms, and she grabs it.
bridge-3 = The small Pokémon she hid floats out: a dark, cloud-like body with yellow eyes, and a glittering blue puff on each side.
bridge-4 = It drifts out onto the bridge, while the girl stops at its end.
bridge-5 = Halfway across, it looks up at the sky.
bridge-6 = High in the sky, three bird Pokémon wheel round.
bridge-7 = They swoop down on it. It shrinks back on the planks as they circle and peck at it.
bridge-8 = You walk up the path to the girl, who stands at the end of the bridge, watching it.
bridge-9 = She turns round to you, clutching her bag.
bridge-10 = The camera looks along the bridge: halfway across, the small Pokémon cowers while the three birds flap and peck at it.
rescue-1 = You run out along the bridge towards the small Pokémon, the birds above.
rescue-2 = You crouch over it, shielding it with your arms.
rescue-3 = A bird dives at you, screeching, claws out.
rescue-4 = Under your arms, the small Pokémon starts to glow.
rescue-5 = A burst of light, and the bridge shatters.
rescue-6 = You fall with the small Pokémon among the broken planks. On the bank, the girl gasps.
rescue-7 = As you fall, a streak of light shoots down past you, scattering the birds.
rescue-8 = Crackling with lightning, a Pokémon catches you in mid-air: an orange crest, and great yellow arms like the halves of a shell.
rescue-9 = On the bank the girl stands alone. The Pokémon lands beside her and sets you down, the small Pokémon in your arms.
rescue-10 = It springs back in a shower of sparks, and stares at you, face to face.
rescue-11 = The girl and you look up at it. It stares a moment longer.
rescue-12 = Then it flares with lightning and is gone, a bolt streaking up into the sky.
rescue-13 = Back on the bank by the broken bridge, the girl and you stand together, the small Pokémon on the ground before you.
rescue-14 = The small Pokémon has floated off a little way, and something glints on the ground beside it.
rescue-15 = An exclamation mark pops up over the girl, and she turns to face you.
rescue-16 = The small Pokémon floats into the girl's bag, and the screen fades.
rescue-17 = The girl sets off down the path, then stops and looks back at you.
